// ============================================================================
//  TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC — add a Label "lblDebug" anywhere on the screen and set
//  its Text to this. It tells you exactly where the pipeline stalls. Delete it
//  once everything works.
//
//  HOW TO READ IT
//  • data = 0  (always)  -> Power BI is sending NO rows to the visual.
//        Fix: in Power BI, add the fields to the PowerApps visual's data well
//        (Name, Crew, User Email, Manager Sponsor Email, and every points column).
//        Nothing here can work until data > 0.
//  • data > 0  but  members = 0  -> the build failed (usually a COLUMN-NAME
//        mismatch). Check the names in tmrLoad exactly match the fields you added,
//        e.g. 'IB & NS Points'. Also confirm tmrLoad fired (toggle started below).
//  • members > 0  but  crews = 0 -> 'Crew' column missing/blank.
//  • members > 0  and the visuals are still blank -> the Image controls aren't
//        seeing the vars; confirm imgMyPoints.Visible = (varRole <> "spectator")
//        and that you pasted the latest Image formulas.
//  • ready = false forever -> tmrLoad never ran: check AutoStart=false,
//        Start = (CountRows(PowerBIIntegration.Data) <> varRowCount), Repeat=false,
//        Duration=50, Visible=true (NOT false), and that the control is on THIS screen.
// ============================================================================
"data=" & CountRows( PowerBIIntegration.Data ) &
" | ready=" & varReady &
" | started=" & tmrLoad.Start &
" | members=" & CountRows( colMembers ) &
" | crews=" & CountRows( colCrew ) &
" | role=" & varRole &
" | me=" & varDispName &
" | email=" & varUserEmail
